{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CggKarvMxg2msd3EVZbiH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The hotfix is applied in `money.py`, and all 4 tests pass. I did not commit or push, since you only asked for the fix to be applied.\n\n**The bug:** `split_cents` used `total // people` and gave every person that same amount, so the `total % people` remainder was dropped. For `(100, 3)` that gave `[33, 33, 33]`, one grosz short.\n\n**The fix** (`money.py`):\n```python\nshare, remainder = divmod(total, people)\nreturn [share + 1 if i < remainder else share for i in range(people)]\n```\nThe first `remainder` people each get one extra grosz, so the shares always sum to `total`.\n\n**Regression test** (`test_money.py`): I added `test_uneven_split_keeps_every_grosz`, which asserts `split_cents(100, 3) == [34, 33, 33]`. I ran it before the fix and it failed (99 != 100), then ran it after and it passed. Your next-sprint backfill is already covered by this test, so it doesn't need to wait.\n\n**Spot checks:** `(100, 3)` → `[34, 33, 33]`, `(0, 4)` → `[0, 0, 0, 0]`, `(7, 7)` → seven 1s, and `(12345, 7)` sums back to 12345.\n\n**Decision for you:** the one-liner is a bit more than a one-liner, but it's still small. The new ordering puts the extra grosz on the first people in the list. If the business needs a different rule for who pays the extra grosz, tell me and I'll change it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":990,"cache_read_input_tokens":22464,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":990},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fdb4d199-a784-40d6-be64-2612821539da","uuid":"dc663191-af37-4d68-a787-5696c63f909a","timest